{"previous_attempts": "Previous attempts refer to earlier efforts and methodologies that have been employed to address a specific problem or challenge. In the context of credit fraud detection, these attempts encompass various strategies and models that researchers and practitioners have developed to identify fraudulent activities within financial transactions."},
{"previous_attempts__use__deep_learning_models": "The use of deep learning models in previous attempts signifies the adoption and application of advanced machine learning techniques to tackle the problem of credit fraud detection. These models, which include Long Short-Term Memory networks (LSTM), Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN), and Bayesian Neural Networks, are utilized to process and analyze transaction data, aiming to improve the accuracy and effectiveness of fraud detection systems."},
{"deep_learning_models": "Deep learning models are a class of machine learning algorithms that use neural networks with multiple layers to extract and learn complex patterns from data. In the context of credit fraud detection, these models are employed to analyze large datasets of financial transactions, identify fraudulent patterns, and make predictions about the likelihood of fraud. The use of deep learning models represents an advanced approach to enhancing the performance and reliability of fraud detection systems."},
