{"some__use__long_short_term_memory_network_lstm": "Use indicates the application or employment of a specific method or technology to achieve a certain goal. In this context, it describes how certain previous attempts have utilized a particular type of neural network to tackle the problem of credit fraud detection."},
{"long_short_term_memory_network_lstm": "Long short term memory network (LSTM) is a type of recurrent neural network (RNN) architecture used in the field of deep learning. Unlike standard feedforward neural networks, LSTM has feedback connections, making it capable of learning and remembering over long sequences of data, which is particularly useful for tasks involving time series prediction and sequence generation."},
{"others": "In the context of credit fraud detection, 'others' refers to researchers or practitioners who have explored various deep learning models to address the challenge of identifying fraudulent transactions within a dataset.|Here is another description: In the context of credit fraud detection, 'others' refers to researchers or practitioners who have explored various deep learning models to address the challenge of detecting fraudulent activities in financial transactions."},
{"others__use__convolutional_neural_network": "The term 'use' in this context signifies the application or employment of a specific deep learning model, namely the convolutional neural network, by researchers or practitioners in their attempts to detect credit fraud."},
{"convolutional_neural_network": "Convolutional neural network (CNN) is a class of deep learning models that have been utilized in credit fraud detection. CNNs are particularly known for their ability to automatically and adaptively learn spatial hierarchies of features from input data, making them suitable for handling complex patterns and relationships within datasets.|Here is another description: Convolutional neural network, a type of deep learning model, is characterized by its use of convolutional layers to automatically and adaptively learn spatial hierarchies of features from input data. In this context, it is specifically a two-layer MLP with two 1D convolutional layers, each having a kernel size of 29.|Here is another description: The convolutional neural network in this context refers to a type of neural network architecture that incorporates convolutional layers to process input data, typically used for tasks like image recognition. In this project, it is specifically configured with additional layers for a particular application.|Here is another description: The convolutional neural network in this context refers to a type of neural network architecture that is being compared against other baseline models in a project. It is characterized by its use of convolutional layers to process input data."},
{"others__use__bayesian_neural_network": "The term 'use' in this context signifies the adoption or application of a specific deep learning model, namely the Bayesian neural network, by researchers or practitioners in their efforts to improve the accuracy and effectiveness of credit fraud detection systems."},
{"bayesian_neural_network": "A Bayesian neural network is a type of deep learning model that incorporates Bayesian inference to estimate the uncertainty in its predictions. This approach allows the model to provide more reliable and interpretable results, which can be particularly useful in applications like credit fraud detection where the consequences of incorrect predictions can be significant."},
{"this_paper__select__aforementioned_models_as_baselines": "The predicate \"select\" in this context means that the paper has chosen specific models to serve as baselines for comparison with the proposed model. This selection is crucial for benchmarking the performance of the new approach."},
{"aforementioned_models_as_baselines": "The aforementioned models as baselines include various deep learning models previously used for credit fraud detection, such as Long Short-Term Memory networks (LSTM), Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN), and Bayesian Neural Networks. These models are chosen to provide a standard for comparing the effectiveness of the proposed approach."},
