{"first_part__filter_out__features_with_low_importance_by_random_forest_regressor": "The action of filtering out involves removing or excluding certain elements from a set based on specific criteria. In this context, it means eliminating features that are deemed less significant for the model's performance."},
{"features_with_low_importance_by_random_forest_regressor": "Features with low importance by Random Forest regressor are those attributes or variables in the dataset that the Random Forest algorithm determines to have minimal impact on the model's predictive accuracy. These features are considered less relevant for detecting credit fraud in this specific context."},
{"second_part": "The second part of the proposed approach in the project, which follows the initial feature filtering by a Random Forest regressor."},
{"second_part__train__deep_learning_method_based_on_transformer_structure": "The action of training or implementing a specific model or method as part of a multi-step approach to solve a problem, in this case, detecting credit fraud."},
{"deep_learning_method_based_on_transformer_structure": "A deep learning method based on the Transformer structure, which is trained in the second part of the project to detect credit fraud after the feature filtering process."},
{"approach": "The approach refers to a proposed method in the paper that combines machine learning algorithms and deep learning methods to detect credit fraud. It involves filtering out features with low importance using a Random Forest regressor and training a deep learning model based on a Transformer structure."},
{"approach__tested_on__public_data_set_with_492_fraud_samples_out_of_284_807_transactions": "The predicate \"tested on\" indicates that the approach was evaluated or experimented with using a specific dataset. It signifies the action of applying the approach to a given set of data to assess its performance and effectiveness."},
{"public_data_set_with_492_fraud_samples_out_of_284_807_transactions": "The object is a public data set that contains 492 fraud samples out of a total of 284,807 transactions. This dataset was used to test and evaluate the performance of the proposed approach in detecting credit fraud. It provides a real-world scenario for assessing the accuracy and effectiveness of the approach."},
{"performance_evaluation": "Performance evaluation in this context refers to the assessment of how well the proposed model and baseline models detect credit fraud. It involves comparing the effectiveness of different machine learning and deep learning methods in identifying fraudulent transactions within a dataset."},
{"performance_evaluation__uses__accuracy_matrix_and_roc_curve": "The predicate \"uses\" indicates the methodology or tools employed to conduct the performance evaluation. In this case, it specifies that the evaluation relies on specific metrics and visual tools to gauge the model's effectiveness."},
{"accuracy_matrix_and_roc_curve": "The accuracy matrix and ROC curve are tools used to evaluate the performance of fraud detection models. The accuracy matrix provides a detailed breakdown of correct and incorrect predictions, while the ROC curve illustrates the trade-off between the true positive rate and the false positive rate at various threshold settings."},
{"method": "The method refers to a proposed approach that integrates multiple algorithms to verify the authenticity and consistency of transaction details. It is designed to enhance security measures in financial transactions by cross-checking various data points.|Here is another description: The method refers to a proposed approach by researchers that utilizes a decision tree to integrate and apply various algorithms for data validation and outlier detection in financial transactions.|Here is another description: The method refers to a proposed approach that utilizes a decision tree to integrate Luhn\u2019s algorithm and Hunt\u2019s algorithm for validating credit card information.|Here is another description: The method refers to a proposed approach that utilizes a decision tree to integrate Luhn\u2019s algorithm and Hunt\u2019s algorithm for validating card information.|Here is another description: The method refers to a technique proposed by researchers that utilizes a decision tree. This method integrates Luhn\u2019s algorithm and Hunt\u2019s algorithm to evaluate various aspects of a transaction."},
