{"select_the_most_important_features_in_the_data_for_training": "Selecting the most important features in the data for training involves determining which features have the greatest impact on the model's performance and are therefore essential for accurate predictions."},
{"the_feature_filter__filters_out__the_less_important_features_to_reduce_the_noisy_features_of_the_model": "The action of filtering out refers to the process where the feature filter removes or excludes certain elements from the dataset."},
{"the_less_important_features_to_reduce_the_noisy_features_of_the_model": "The less important features are those elements within the dataset that are deemed to have a lower significance or relevance to the model's predictive capabilities, and by filtering them out, the aim is to decrease the amount of noise or irrelevant information that could potentially hinder the model's performance."},
{"the_second_part": "The second part of the model refers to the component that follows the feature filter in the pipeline approach. It is responsible for data optimization and learning after the initial feature selection process."},
