{"above_steps": "The above steps refer to the process of randomly selecting K data samples from the training data to build corresponding decision trees as part of constructing a random forest regression algorithm."},
{"above_steps__iterated__n_times_to_construct_the_random_forest": "The predicate 'iterated' describes the process of repeating the aforementioned steps multiple times to enhance the construction of the random forest. This iteration is crucial for improving the model's predictive accuracy and controlling over-fitting by averaging the results from multiple decision trees."},
{"n_times_to_construct_the_random_forest": "'N times to construct the random forest' indicates the number of iterations performed to build the random forest. Each iteration involves creating a decision tree using a subset of the data, and the final random forest is an ensemble of these N decision trees, which are averaged to produce the final predictions."},
