{"each_feature__put_into__each_decision_tree": "Put into signifies the process of incorporating or inserting each feature into the structure and calculations of the decision trees within the random forest algorithm. This step is crucial for assessing how each feature contributes to the predictions made by each tree."},
{"each_decision_tree": "Each decision tree represents one of the multiple classifying trees within the random forest algorithm. These trees are built on different sub-samples of the dataset and are used collectively to improve predictive accuracy and control over-fitting through averaging their individual predictions."},
{"predicted_values": "The predicted values refer to the outcomes generated by individual decision trees within the random forest algorithm for each feature during the regression process."},
{"predicted_values__averaged_to_get__score_of_the_random_forest": "The process of averaging involves taking the mean of the predicted values from each decision tree to produce a consolidated score, which serves as a measure of feature importance."},
{"score_of_the_random_forest": "The score of the random forest represents the averaged predicted values from all decision trees, indicating the importance weight of each feature, which is subsequently utilized in the neural network for further processing."},
