{"a_fully_connected_neural_network": "A fully connected neural network, also known as a dense network, is a type of artificial neural network where each neuron in one layer is connected to every neuron in the next layer. This architecture allows for complex pattern recognition and is commonly used in various machine learning applications for its ability to model intricate relationships within data."},
{"wful": "Wful is a matrix used in the context of neural network computations, specifically within the framework of a bidirectional LSTM network. It plays a crucial role in the transformation and processing of input data by applying weights to the inputs, which are then combined with a bias matrix and passed through an activation function."},
