{"a_position_wise_fully_connected_feed_forward_network": "A position-wise fully-connected feed forward network is a type of neural network layer that applies a linear transformation to each position separately, followed by a non-linear activation function. It is used to map the input features to a higher dimensional space, enhancing the model's ability to capture complex patterns.|Here is another description: A position-wise fully-connected feed forward network is a type of neural network layer used in transformer models. It applies a linear transformation followed by a non-linear activation function to each position independently, allowing the model to learn complex relationships between input features."},
