{"loss_function": "A loss function, in the context of machine learning, is a method of evaluating how well specific algorithms perform by estimating the difference between the predicted and actual values. It guides the optimization process to improve the model's accuracy.|Here is another description: The loss function, specifically a binary cross entropy loss in this context, is a method used to evaluate how well the model's predictions match the actual outcomes. It quantifies the difference between the predicted and true values."},
