{"transactions_that_occurred_in_two_days": "The transactions that occurred in two days refer to a subset of the dataset containing credit card transactions from a specific two-day period in September 2013. This subset includes a total of 284,807 transactions, with 492 of them being fraud samples."},
{"dataset__contains__492_fraud_samples_out_of_284_807_transactions": "The predicate \"contains\" indicates the presence of a specific number of fraud samples within the larger set of transactions in the dataset. This relation highlights the dataset's composition and the proportion of fraudulent activities relative to legitimate transactions."},
{"492_fraud_samples_out_of_284_807_transactions": "The object \"492 fraud samples out of 284,807 transactions\" specifies the exact number of fraudulent transactions within the dataset, emphasizing the dataset's unbalance with frauds accounting for only 0.172% of all transactions. This detail is crucial for understanding the dataset's characteristics and the challenges it presents for analysis."},
