{"transformed_with_pca": "PCA, or Principal Component Analysis, is a dimensionality reduction technique used to transform a large set of variables into a smaller one that still contains most of the information in the large set. In this context, it refers to the transformation that was applied to the other features in the dataset but not to Time and Amount."},
