{"transaction_amount": "The transaction Amount is a specific financial metric representing the sum of money involved in a transaction. It is a critical feature in datasets related to financial transactions, especially in the context of fraud detection."},
{"transaction_amount__can_be_used_for__example_dependant_cost_sensitive_learning": "The phrase \"can be used for\" indicates a utility or application of the subject in a particular context or process. In this case, it suggests that the transaction Amount has a specific use or function within a certain type of machine learning approach."},
{"example_dependant_cost_sensitive_learning": "Example-dependant cost-sensitive learning is a machine learning technique where the cost of misclassification varies depending on the specific instance or example. This approach is particularly useful in scenarios where different errors have different costs, such as in fraud detection, where the cost of missing a fraudulent transaction is significantly higher than incorrectly flagging a legitimate one."},
{"feature_class": "Feature Class refers to a category or classification of features within a dataset, specifically used in the context of fraud detection. It is a critical element in machine learning models that aim to predict fraudulent activities based on various input features.|Here is another description: Feature Class is identified as the response variable in a dataset, particularly relevant in the context of fraud detection. It serves as a critical indicator within the dataset, helping to classify transactions based on their characteristics."},
