{"the_response_variable": "The response variable in a dataset is the target variable that the model aims to predict or explain. In the context of fraud detection, the response variable, Feature Class, takes the value 1 if fraud is detected and 0 otherwise, serving as the outcome of the predictive model."},
{"feature_class__takes_value__1_in_case_of_fraud_and_0_otherwise": "The predicate \"takes value\" describes the action or state that the Feature Class assumes within the dataset. It indicates the specific values that Feature Class can adopt, which are crucial for determining the nature of transactions."},
