{"credit_card_fraud": "Credit card fraud is a significant issue within the financial sector, involving unauthorized use of credit card information for illicit transactions. It has become a major concern for both consumers and financial institutions due to the potential for substantial financial loss and identity theft.|Here is another description: Credit card fraud is a type of financial crime where fraudsters use stolen or counterfeit credit card information to make unauthorized transactions. This form of fraud has become increasingly prevalent as credit cards have grown in popularity as a payment method."},
{"credit_card_fraud__has_grabbed__a_lot_of_attention_in_data_science_domain": "The phrase \"has grabbed\" indicates that credit card fraud has captured or attracted significant interest and focus. In this context, it highlights the increasing importance and attention that the issue of credit card fraud has received, particularly within the data science community."},
{"a_lot_of_attention_in_data_science_domain": "\"A lot of attention in data science domain\" refers to the substantial interest and focus that credit card fraud has garnered among data scientists and researchers. This attention is driven by the need to develop effective methods and models to detect and prevent fraudulent activities, leveraging advancements in machine learning and data analytics."},
{"most_previous_works": "Most previous works refer to the majority of earlier research and studies conducted in the field of credit card fraud detection using data science techniques.|Here is another description: Most previous works refer to the majority of earlier research efforts and studies conducted in the field of credit card fraud detection using data science techniques."},
{"most_previous_works__tackled__this_problem": "The predicate 'tackled' indicates that the previous works addressed or attempted to solve the problem of credit card fraud using specific methodologies, primarily machine learning methods with hand-crafted features."},
