{"\u03c3__can_be__any_activation_function": "The predicate \"can be\" indicates the flexibility in choosing an activation function for the neural network model, allowing for various options depending on the specific requirements or preferences of the task at hand."},
{"any_activation_function": "Any activation function refers to the broad category of functions that can be selected to introduce non-linearity into the model, enabling it to learn complex patterns and make accurate predictions. Examples include ReLU, sigmoid, and tanh, among others."},
