{"bidirectional_lstm_network": "The bidirectional LSTM network is a type of recurrent neural network that processes input sequences in both forward and backward directions. This allows it to capture dependencies and context from both past and future elements within the sequence, enhancing its ability to understand and predict complex patterns."},
{"bidirectional_lstm_network__is_introduced__to_map_the_features": "The phrase \"is introduced\" signifies that the bidirectional LSTM network is being presented or implemented within the context of the model to perform a specific function. This introduction is aimed at improving the model's capability to handle sequential data effectively."},
{"to_map_the_features": "To map the features refers to the process of transforming input data into a more meaningful or useful representation. In this context, the bidirectional LSTM network is used to convert raw sequential data into a format that better captures the underlying patterns and relationships, making it easier for subsequent layers or models to interpret and utilize."},
{"common_lstm_unit": "A common LSTM unit is a fundamental component of Long Short-Term Memory networks, designed to process sequential data by maintaining and regulating information flow over time."},
{"common_lstm_unit__is_composed_of__a_cell_an_input_gate_an_output_gate_and_a_forget_gate": "The phrase \"is composed of\" indicates the structural makeup of the common LSTM unit, detailing the specific elements that constitute its architecture."},
{"a_cell_an_input_gate_an_output_gate_and_a_forget_gate": "The components\u2014a cell, an input gate, an output gate, and a forget gate\u2014are essential parts of the LSTM unit. The cell stores values over time, while the gates control the flow of information into, out of, and within the cell, enabling the LSTM to effectively manage and utilize temporal dependencies in data."},
{"the_cell": "The cell is a fundamental component of a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) unit, which is part of a bidirectional LSTM network used for mapping features and processing sequential data."},
{"the_cell__remembers__values_over_arbitrary_time_intervals": "The predicate \"remembers\" in this context refers to the cell's capability to retain information over extended periods, which is crucial for handling time series data where significant events may be separated by unknown durations."},
{"values_over_arbitrary_time_intervals": "Values over arbitrary time intervals refer to the data points or information that the LSTM cell is designed to store and recall, regardless of the time gap between them, enabling effective processing and classification of time-dependent sequences."},
{"the_three_gates": "The three gates refer to the input gate, output gate, and forget gate within a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) unit. These gates are essential components that help manage the flow of information in the LSTM network."},
{"the_three_gates__regulate__the_flow_of_information_into_and_out_of_the_cell": "The predicate'regulate' in this context means that the three gates control or manage the flow of information. They determine how much information is allowed to enter, exit, or be retained within the cell of the LSTM unit."},
{"the_flow_of_information_into_and_out_of_the_cell": "The flow of information into and out of the cell refers to the data that is processed by the LSTM unit. This includes both the input data entering the cell and the output data exiting the cell, which is crucial for the LSTM's ability to make predictions and process time-series data effectively."},
{"lstm": "LSTM, or Long Short-Term Memory, is a type of recurrent neural network (RNN) architecture designed to better capture long-term dependencies and mitigate the vanishing gradient problem often encountered in traditional RNNs. It consists of memory cells and various gates that regulate the flow of information."},
