{"transformer_model": "The Transformer model is a feature extractor based on a multiheaded attention mechanism, originally proposed by Google. It is designed to compute the weighted representation of all input features per unit of time, allowing for parallel computation which reduces both computation cost and time cost. In the given context, only the encoder part of the Transformer is used to extract features from sequential data.|Here is another description: The Transformer model is a sophisticated neural network architecture designed for processing sequential data. It is particularly known for its efficiency in handling long sequences and its ability to perform parallel computations, which significantly reduces training time and computational costs.|Here is another description: The Transformer model is a type of feature extractor that utilizes a multiheaded attention mechanism. It is designed to map sequential features to a higher dimension, allowing for efficient computation and improved capture of sequential data.|Here is another description: The Transformer model is a type of feature extractor that utilizes a multi-headed attention mechanism, originally proposed by Google. It is designed to efficiently process sequential data by computing weighted representations of input features in parallel, which significantly reduces computation and time costs."},
