{"transformer": "The Transformer is a type of model architecture that utilizes a multiheaded attention mechanism to process data. It is known for its efficiency in handling sequential data by allowing parallel computation, which reduces both computation and time costs.|Here is another description: The Transformer is a type of model architecture that utilizes a multiheaded attention mechanism to process input data. It is known for its ability to handle sequential data efficiently by computing representations in parallel.|Here is another description: The Transformer is a type of model architecture that utilizes a multiheaded attention mechanism to process input data. It is known for its ability to handle sequential data efficiently by computing representations in parallel, which is a departure from traditional sequential models like RNNs and CNNs.|Here is another description: The Transformer is a type of model architecture that utilizes a multiheaded attention mechanism to process input data. It is known for its ability to handle sequential data efficiently by computing representations in parallel, which reduces computational and time costs."},
