{"logits": "Logits are raw, unnormalized scores output by a model, representing the model's confidence in each class before applying a softmax or sigmoid function. In this context, logits are the values generated for each training sample that will be processed further to make a classification decision.|Here is another description: Logits are the raw, unnormalized scores output by a model before they are passed through a function like softmax or sigmoid to convert them into probabilities. In the context of fraud detection, logits represent the model's initial assessment of whether a given sample is fraudulent or not.|Here is another description: Logits are the raw, unnormalized scores output by a model before they are passed through a function like sigmoid to convert them into probabilities. In the context of fraud detection, logits represent the model's initial assessment of whether a given sample is fraudulent or not."},
