{"om_prakash_patel": "Om Prakash Patel is a researcher and author known for his significant contributions to the field of machine learning, particularly in the area of credit card fraud detection. He has co-authored multiple papers on the comparative study of machine learning techniques for detecting credit card fraud, collaborating with various researchers including Dong-Lin Li, Chandan Jha, Neha Bharill, Sudhanshu Joshi, Deepak Puthal, and Mukesh Prasad. His work focuses on evaluating the performance of different machine learning algorithms in identifying fraudulent credit card transactions, with a particular emphasis on the effects of time variance on fraud detection algorithms. Patel's contributions have been presented at notable conferences such as the 2018 IEEE Symposium Series on Computational Intelligence."},
{"shantanu_rajora__co_author__sudhanshu_joshi": "The predicate \"co-author\" signifies that Shantanu Rajora and Sudhanshu Joshi collaborated on the research paper, contributing jointly to its content and findings.|Here is another description: The predicate \"co-author\" indicates a collaborative relationship between two or more individuals who have jointly contributed to the creation of a research paper or publication. In this context, it signifies that Shantanu Rajora and Sudhanshu Joshi have worked together as co-authors on the specified research paper."},
{"sudhanshu_joshi": "Sudhanshu Joshi is a researcher and author specializing in machine learning techniques for credit card fraud detection. He has co-authored multiple studies on the topic, collaborating with various researchers including Shantanu Rajora, Dong-Lin Li, Chandan Jha, Neha Bharill, Om Prakash Patel, Mukesh Prasad, and others. His work, which involves applying computational intelligence techniques to real-world fraud detection problems, has been presented at the 2018 IEEE Symposium Series on Computational Intelligence (SSCI). Joshi's contributions are part of collaborative efforts to advance knowledge in detecting fraudulent activities in credit card transactions."},
